SUMMARY:Visible Labour - Group Show Featuring Five Women Artists
DESCRIPTION:“Visible Labour” presents the work of 5 women artists who meet to discuss their work\, exposing it to each other’s sensibilities as a counterweight to artistic isolation. The work in the exhibition has emerged from their individual practices\, using a breadth of techniques; however\, the sharing is collective\, visually intelligent and sustained. The Leslie Grove Gallery from April 29-May 10. Gallery hours: Wednesday to Sunday 12-5 PM.  Opening reception will take place on Sunday\, May 3\, 1-5 pm. Details at https://www.artistsnetwork.ca/patrons-calendar.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/visible-labour-group-show-featuring-five-women-artists/
LOCATION:1158 Queen Street East\, 1158 Queen St E\, Toronto\, ON M4M 1L2\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M4M 1L2
CATEGORIES:Art & Design,Exhibitions
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/visible-labour-group-show-featuring-five-women-artists.png
END:VEVENT
