SUMMARY:Open Studio
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Open Studio hosted by Re-Work\, a space to explore your creativity\, connect with others\, and simply create without judgment. Whether you want to doodle\, colour\, write\, or just relax\, this is your time to do what inspires you\, alongside like-minded folks. \n​​​Open Studio is more than a creative outlet. It’s a place to find rest\, connection\, and a little relief from daily pressures—a communal experience rooted in care and play. \n​​​✨ A portion of proceeds from each will be donated to the Parkdale Food Bank\, supporting nourishment and community care in our neighbourhood. \n​​​Let’s create together. \nAbout Re-Work\n​Re-Work is a Community First \n​We’re a professional (and personal) development community helping people redefine work\, ambition\, and success on their own terms. We want you to get to a healthier\, less stress-filled place with the thing we spend most of our lives doing: working. Move beyond burnout toward work that is meaningful and fulfilling as your fullest self. Through a proven process and framework\, we help you craft a more sustainable and values-aligned relationship with work. Through workshops\, storytelling\, and community spaces\, Re-Work invites you to explore a healthier\, more sustainable way of working and living. \n​Let’s build a future of work that works for you.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/open-studio/
LOCATION:Issues Magazine Shop\, 1489 Dundas St W\, Toronto\, ON M6K 1T6\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M6K 1T6
CATEGORIES:Art & Design,Classes & Workshops
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/open-studio.png
END:VEVENT
