SUMMARY:Pascuala Ilabaca & Fauna
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Small World Music and Lula Music and Arts Centre \nAccordion-wielding Chilean songstress Pascuala Ilabaca is a true hidden gem. A favourite on the vibrant scene of young Chilean singer-songwriters\, her music is rooted in traditional sounds but effortlessly integrates shades of jazz\, pop\, and rock\, with influences gathered from places as distant as India and Mexico. \nAccompanied by her formidable band Fauna\, Ilabaca’s unique stage presence conjures up sweetness and empowerment while simultaneously setting her songs alive with both fragility and verve. Her performance bridges the folkloric roots of the Andes with a contemporary global edge. \nAbout the Artist: Pascuala Ilabaca is a singer-songwriter hailing from Valparaiso\, Chile. Her debut album\, Pascuala Canta a Violeta\, was released in 2008\, featuring her arrangements of legendary singer-songwriter Violeta Parra’s songs. \nIn 2010\, Ilabaca received the Guitarpin de Oro prize at the Festival del Huaso de Olmué\, and by 2012\, she had completed her first two European tours. In 2013\, Ilabaca and her band Fauna were the Audience Award winners for Best World Beat Album at the Independent Music Awards. They have graced prestigious stages worldwide\, including the Music and Politics Festival in Berlin\, Barnasants Festival in Barcelona\, and the London Jazz Festival. \nHer career reached new heights in 2016 when she received the Pulsar Prize\, the most important Chilean music industry award. Following the release of her acclaimed album El mito de la pergola in 2018\, she has spent the last several years touring extensively across Chile\, Europe\, Colombia\, and the United States\, solidifying her reputation as one of the most unique and treasured voices in the Latin American and global music scenes. \nFor Lula dining reservations\, please visit https://www.lula.ca/reservations \nDoors open at 7:00pm \nFor general inquiries or accessibility requests\, please email us at boxoffice@smallworldmusic.com or call us at 416-536-5439. \nThe 2026 Small World Music Series is sponsored by TD Bank Group through the TD Ready Commitment and funded by the Government of Canada\, Canada Council for the Arts\, Ontario Arts Council\, and the City of Toronto through the Toronto Arts Council.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/pascuala-ilabaca-fauna-2/
LOCATION:Lula Lounge\, 1585 Dundas St W\, Toronto\, M6K 1T9
CATEGORIES:Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/pascuala-ilabaca-fauna-1.png
END:VEVENT
